WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.531 --> 00:02.666 align:center line:81%
This general conference of October

00:02.666 --> 00:09.273 align:center line:79%
2025 marks the 30th anniversary
of the announcement of “The Family:

00:09.273 --> 00:13.277 align:center line:79%
A Proclamation to the World.”
By divine design,

00:13.277 --> 00:17.080 align:center line:79%
this proclamation,
with its revelatory words,

00:17.180 --> 00:19.449 align:center line:81%
was created to “maintain

00:19.449 --> 00:24.354 align:center line:79%
and strengthen the family
as the fundamental unit of society.”

00:25.422 --> 00:31.028 align:center line:79%
Everyone belongs to a family, whether
you are a mother, father, daughter, son,

00:31.161 --> 00:37.267 align:center line:79%
grandchild, grandparent,
aunt, uncle, brother, sister, or cousin.

00:37.901 --> 00:44.541 align:center line:79%
Most importantly, each of us are, as the
proclamation states, “a beloved spirit

00:44.541 --> 00:50.814 align:center line:79%
son or daughter of heavenly parents ...
[with] a divine nature and destiny.”

00:52.215 --> 00:56.320 align:center line:79%
When I was called
to the holy apostleship in 2015,

00:56.687 --> 01:00.991 align:center line:79%
I was advised, “This proclamation
is now yours.

01:01.458 --> 01:06.363 align:center line:79%
Your name,” pointing to the words
“Council of the Twelve Apostles”

01:06.563 --> 01:08.932 align:center line:81%
in the title, “is right here.

01:09.399 --> 01:13.070 align:center line:81%
Feel it and teach it like you own it.”

01:14.271 --> 01:16.907 align:center line:81%
I love the family proclamation.

01:17.207 --> 01:19.776 align:center line:81%
I have testified across the world,

01:19.776 --> 01:24.247 align:center line:79%
from Africa to Australia
and everywhere in between,

01:24.681 --> 01:28.185 align:center line:79%
of the role of the family
in God's eternal plan.

01:28.986 --> 01:31.822 align:center line:81%
The proclamation has a divine origin,

01:32.155 --> 01:37.027 align:center line:79%
so we must treat it with the reverence
deserving words from God.

01:38.562 --> 01:40.397 align:center line:81%
Remember, brothers and sisters,

01:40.597 --> 01:46.303 align:center line:79%
as I said in a previous general conference
from this very pulpit, “words matter.”

01:47.170 --> 01:50.507 align:center line:79%
Let me give you some background
about the proclamation

01:50.507 --> 01:53.677 align:center line:81%
as a core message of what we believe.

01:54.811 --> 01:59.716 align:center line:79%
In 1994, a year before the
proclamation was presented,

01:59.950 --> 02:04.388 align:center line:79%
the Quorum of the Twelve
Apostles discussed how society

02:04.388 --> 02:09.760 align:center line:79%
and governments were pulling away
from God's laws of family, marriage,

02:09.760 --> 02:14.264 align:center line:79%
and gender. “But that was not
the end of what we saw,”

02:14.564 --> 02:17.601 align:center line:79%
President Russell M. Nelson
later explained.

02:18.101 --> 02:23.874 align:center line:79%
“We could see the efforts of various
communities to do away with all standards

02:23.874 --> 02:27.310 align:center line:81%
and limitations on sexual activity.

02:27.811 --> 02:30.280 align:center line:81%
We saw the confusion of genders.

02:30.580 --> 02:32.816 align:center line:81%
We could see it all coming.”

02:34.484 --> 02:37.354 align:center line:79%
The Twelve determined to
prepare a document,

02:37.521 --> 02:43.160 align:center line:79%
an official proclamation, summarizing
the Church’s position on family.

02:43.894 --> 02:47.597 align:center line:79%
During that year,
these apostles, seers called

02:47.597 --> 02:51.601 align:center line:79%
of God, prepared a declaration
about the family.

02:52.402 --> 02:54.805 align:center line:81%
President Dallin H. Oaks recalled,

02:54.805 --> 02:59.209 align:center line:79%
they prayerfully turned
to the Lord for “what [they] should say

02:59.476 --> 03:01.278 align:center line:81%
and how [they] should say it.”

03:02.279 --> 03:04.414 align:center line:81%
They presented the First Presidency

03:04.715 --> 03:10.053 align:center line:79%
the proclamation—Presidents Howard
W. Hunter, Gordon B. Hinckley,

03:10.053 --> 03:13.724 align:center line:79%
and Thomas S. Monson—
for their consideration.

03:14.558 --> 03:18.295 align:center line:81%
Just months later in March 1995,

03:18.695 --> 03:20.597 align:center line:81%
President Hunter passed away,

03:20.964 --> 03:25.402 align:center line:79%
and President Hinckley
became the 15th president of the Church.

03:26.903 --> 03:29.473 align:center line:81%
The proclamation was now in his hands.

03:30.073 --> 03:34.544 align:center line:79%
When would be the right time
to make this declaration to the Church?

03:35.312 --> 03:37.814 align:center line:81%
That time came six months later.

03:38.548 --> 03:43.186 align:center line:79%
Days before the September 23rd
General Women’s meeting

03:43.353 --> 03:45.489 align:center line:81%
that preceded general conference,

03:45.789 --> 03:49.860 align:center line:79%
President Hinckley
and his counselors met in council

03:49.860 --> 03:52.729 align:center line:79%
with the Relief Society
General Presidency.

03:53.663 --> 03:56.333 align:center line:81%
The sisters, like the apostles,

03:56.500 --> 04:00.771 align:center line:79%
had been weighing concerns
about women and families.

04:01.571 --> 04:05.575 align:center line:79%
They had focused the upcoming
meeting on families.

04:06.510 --> 04:10.781 align:center line:79%
President Hinckley was scheduled
to address the women at the gathering.

04:11.281 --> 04:14.785 align:center line:79%
He had been pondering
the direction of his remarks.

04:15.952 --> 04:21.424 align:center line:79%
As the discussion progressed,
he referred by name to the newly created,

04:21.424 --> 04:26.229 align:center line:79%
but not yet public, “The Family:
A Proclamation to the World.”

04:26.997 --> 04:29.733 align:center line:81%
Was this women's meeting the right setting

04:29.766 --> 04:34.037 align:center line:79%
to make the decisive
declaration about family?

04:35.405 --> 04:40.210 align:center line:79%
General Relief Society President
Elaine Jack later explained:

04:40.677 --> 04:45.182 align:center line:79%
“We didn’t know what the proclamation
on the family was at the time.

04:45.615 --> 04:47.484 align:center line:81%
[W]e could tell by the title,

04:47.851 --> 04:51.955 align:center line:79%
but we felt anything on the family ...
would be a positive thing. ...

04:52.589 --> 04:56.593 align:center line:79%
It felt very positive
that we had members of the Quorum

04:56.593 --> 05:00.297 align:center line:79%
of the Twelve that were
receiving revelation.”

05:01.598 --> 05:05.602 align:center line:79%
The Relief Society
meeting that Saturday was historic.

05:06.036 --> 05:09.539 align:center line:79%
President Hinckley
introduced the family proclamation

05:09.739 --> 05:12.042 align:center line:81%
with these important words:

05:13.476 --> 05:17.214 align:center line:79%
“With so much sophistry
that has passed off as truth,

05:17.514 --> 05:22.085 align:center line:79%
with so much of deception
concerning standards and values,

05:22.419 --> 05:24.454 align:center line:81%
with so much of allurement

05:24.454 --> 05:28.825 align:center line:79%
and enticement to take
on the slow stain of the world,

05:29.125 --> 05:33.430 align:center line:79%
we have felt to warn
and forewarn ... of standards,

05:33.496 --> 05:40.337 align:center line:79%
doctrines, and practices relative
to the family which the prophets, seers,

05:40.337 --> 05:46.576 align:center line:79%
and revelators of this Church have
repeatedly stated throughout its history.”

05:47.777 --> 05:50.881 align:center line:79%
He then read the proclamation
in its entirety.

05:51.948 --> 05:53.583 align:center line:81%
As the Lord has said,

05:53.884 --> 06:00.390 align:center line:79%
“Whether by mine own voice or by
the voice of my servants, it is the same.”

06:01.725 --> 06:06.696 align:center line:79%
The proclamation states,
“The family is ordained of God.”

06:07.731 --> 06:10.767 align:center line:81%
I love the clarity of that statement.

06:11.501 --> 06:15.205 align:center line:79%
The proclamation is a call
for us to live in mortality,

06:15.505 --> 06:19.042 align:center line:81%
ever mindful of the divinity within us

06:19.409 --> 06:23.113 align:center line:79%
and the eternal
future that lies before us.

06:23.680 --> 06:28.718 align:center line:79%
President Nelson taught, “you are
literally spirit children of God. ...

06:29.085 --> 06:31.154 align:center line:81%
Make no mistake about it:

06:31.354 --> 06:33.723 align:center line:81%
Your potential is divine.

06:34.190 --> 06:40.263 align:center line:79%
With your diligent seeking, God will give
you glimpses of who you may become.”

06:41.865 --> 06:48.505 align:center line:79%
When presented, the proclamation
did not align with the views of many

06:48.505 --> 06:53.109 align:center line:81%
in the world. Not then. Not now.

06:54.277 --> 06:57.147 align:center line:79%
There are those who take issue
with the declaration

06:57.147 --> 06:59.883 align:center line:81%
on family, marriage and gender.

07:00.684 --> 07:04.921 align:center line:79%
Some suggest the Church
pull it back, revise,

07:05.155 --> 07:07.791 align:center line:81%
or even set the proclamation aside.

07:09.359 --> 07:15.699 align:center line:79%
The proclamation on the family is,
as President Hinckley stated, doctrine,

07:16.032 --> 07:21.271 align:center line:79%
my dear brothers and sisters. The
principles are not out-of-step

07:21.471 --> 07:27.210 align:center line:79%
but perfectly in-step with the ways
of the Lord and his covenant path.

07:28.044 --> 07:32.949 align:center line:79%
The teachings of the proclamation
were revealed by our Lord Jesus Christ

07:32.983 --> 07:35.085 align:center line:81%
to his apostles then

07:36.219 --> 07:37.220 align:center line:81%
and now.

07:38.455 --> 07:44.828 align:center line:79%
This is His Church; He has established
the truths by which we live.

07:46.096 --> 07:49.933 align:center line:79%
Some of you may reflect on the
proclamation and say,

07:50.066 --> 07:52.369 align:center line:81%
“This isn’t working for me.”

07:52.369 --> 07:54.204 align:center line:81%
“It seems insensitive.”

07:54.604 --> 07:56.940 align:center line:81%
“My family doesn’t look like that.”

07:57.240 --> 07:58.641 align:center line:81%
“I don’t fit.”

07:59.743 --> 08:01.811 align:center line:81%
For those with concerns,

08:02.579 --> 08:05.815 align:center line:79%
know that you are a child
of heavenly parents,

08:06.082 --> 08:08.651 align:center line:81%
part of your Heavenly Father's family.

08:09.252 --> 08:14.424 align:center line:79%
No one knows you better or cares
more deeply about you than He does.

08:15.058 --> 08:18.361 align:center line:81%
Turn to Him, pour out your heart to Him,

08:18.762 --> 08:20.930 align:center line:81%
trust Him and His promises.

08:21.731 --> 08:25.635 align:center line:79%
You have family in your Savior
Jesus Christ, who loves you.

08:26.169 --> 08:32.575 align:center line:79%
He came to earth to atone for our sins
and bear the burden of our mistakes

08:32.742 --> 08:34.744 align:center line:81%
and our very bad days.

08:35.478 --> 08:38.915 align:center line:79%
He understands what
you are facing and feeling.

08:39.382 --> 08:43.987 align:center line:79%
Turn to Him, trust He will send
the Holy Ghost to be with you,

08:44.220 --> 08:46.222 align:center line:81%
lift you, and guide you.

08:46.856 --> 08:51.161 align:center line:79%
Feel Their love that “sheddeth
itself abroad in the hearts

08:51.161 --> 08:52.595 align:center line:81%
of the children of men; ...

08:53.063 --> 08:59.135 align:center line:79%
it is the most desirable above all
things ... and the most joyous to the

08:59.135 --> 09:00.370 align:center line:81%
soul.”

09:01.438 --> 09:05.475 align:center line:79%
All of the Lord’s
Apostles love you dearly.

09:06.676 --> 09:11.614 align:center line:79%
We pray for you and seek
the Lord’s guidance for you.

09:12.649 --> 09:13.950 align:center line:81%
Stay with us.

09:14.984 --> 09:19.656 align:center line:79%
You live in challenging times when
the adversary seeks to make you his.

09:20.256 --> 09:27.630 align:center line:79%
Do not be drawn off. And if you are, come
back. Our arms reach out to you,

09:27.964 --> 09:31.134 align:center line:81%
as will those others who love you.

09:32.035 --> 09:38.241 align:center line:79%
The proclamation states, “Parents
have a sacred duty to rear

09:38.241 --> 09:41.111 align:center line:81%
their children in love and righteousness.”

09:41.845 --> 09:45.849 align:center line:79%
The Book of Mormon provides
a second witness to this truth.

09:47.016 --> 09:52.355 align:center line:79%
In the first verse of the first
chapter, we read: “I, Nephi,

09:52.655 --> 09:55.191 align:center line:81%
having been born of goodly parents.”

09:56.126 --> 10:01.397 align:center line:79%
How many of us have started the Book
of Mormon, and started again and again,

10:01.965 --> 10:08.404 align:center line:79%
and in the process committed those words
to memory? Commit them to heart.

10:09.539 --> 10:15.011 align:center line:79%
One of my favorite statements
in the proclamation is this:

10:15.078 --> 10:19.215 align:center line:79%
“Happiness in family life is most
likely to be achieved

10:19.215 --> 10:26.089 align:center line:79%
when founded upon the teachings of Jesus
Christ.” Who does not want to be happy?

10:27.090 --> 10:29.792 align:center line:79%
And what are the teachings
of Jesus Christ?

10:30.260 --> 10:36.699 align:center line:79%
Again, in the proclamation: “Faith,
prayer, repentance, forgiveness, respect,

10:36.699 --> 10:42.038 align:center line:79%
love, compassion, work,
and wholesome recreational activities.”

10:43.306 --> 10:47.911 align:center line:79%
Whose life will not be better
by applying these key principles?

10:48.711 --> 10:51.614 align:center line:81%
None of us are going to do perfectly,

10:52.115 --> 10:55.218 align:center line:79%
but we can follow
President Hinckley’s

10:55.218 --> 10:58.922 align:center line:81%
wise words: “Do the very best you can.”

10:59.956 --> 11:05.195 align:center line:79%
We read in the proclamation: “Fathers are
to preside ... in love and righteousness,”

11:05.562 --> 11:10.733 align:center line:79%
and “mothers are primarily responsible
for the nurture of their children.”

11:11.801 --> 11:18.508 align:center line:79%
Preside does not mean dominate, and
nurture does not mean a secondary role.

11:19.309 --> 11:23.713 align:center line:79%
God has given men and women
different but equal

11:23.713 --> 11:27.450 align:center line:79%
and essential roles
that complement each other.

11:28.885 --> 11:30.787 align:center line:81%
Let me share a personal story.

11:31.554 --> 11:36.459 align:center line:79%
My wife and I learned to work better
at being equal partners

11:36.726 --> 11:39.195 align:center line:81%
after one day when I decided

11:39.195 --> 11:44.367 align:center line:79%
to make an important
decision without consulting her.

11:45.435 --> 11:47.470 align:center line:81%
My actions surprised her,

11:47.904 --> 11:52.642 align:center line:79%
took her off guard, and put
her in a very difficult situation.

11:53.343 --> 12:00.917 align:center line:79%
Afterwards, she put her hands
on my shoulders and firmly said, “Ron,

12:01.384 --> 12:04.721 align:center line:81%
please, never do that to me again.”

12:05.955 --> 12:09.192 align:center line:79%
We've pretty much been on
the same page ever since.

12:11.494 --> 12:14.063 align:center line:81%
We find in the family proclamation:

12:14.430 --> 12:19.669 align:center line:79%
“Fathers and mothers are obligated
to help one another as equal partners.”

12:20.803 --> 12:22.772 align:center line:81%
“Equal” is a word that matters.

12:23.239 --> 12:25.308 align:center line:81%
Over the years as Sister Rasband

12:25.308 --> 12:29.178 align:center line:79%
and I have worked together
in what the proclamation describes

12:29.178 --> 12:32.081 align:center line:81%
as “our sacred responsibilities,”

12:32.081 --> 12:36.319 align:center line:79%
we have shaped an equally
yoked marriage. As each

12:36.319 --> 12:38.454 align:center line:81%
of our children are now married,

12:38.454 --> 12:42.558 align:center line:79%
Sister Rasband and I
have continued to counsel them

12:42.558 --> 12:48.765 align:center line:79%
and their spouses on how to be equal
partners. When we live with our eyes,

12:48.831 --> 12:50.500 align:center line:81%
single to the glory of God,

12:50.900 --> 12:54.470 align:center line:79%
we respect one another
and support one another.

12:54.971 --> 12:59.642 align:center line:79%
Those divine patterns
of righteousness lead to stability

12:59.642 --> 13:05.348 align:center line:79%
in our individual lives,
and our families, and in society.

13:06.249 --> 13:10.787 align:center line:79%
Our Father in Heaven has provided
the proclamation on the family

13:10.787 --> 13:13.089 align:center line:81%
to help guide us come home to Him,

13:13.523 --> 13:16.659 align:center line:79%
to help us learn to be filled
with love and strength,

13:16.926 --> 13:19.429 align:center line:81%
purpose, and eternal understanding.

13:20.363 --> 13:26.602 align:center line:79%
With all my soul, I plead with you
to live close to Him and His Beloved Son.

13:27.103 --> 13:29.072 align:center line:81%
I promise as you do so,

13:29.305 --> 13:31.874 align:center line:81%
the Spirit will inspire and guide you

13:31.874 --> 13:37.680 align:center line:79%
and help you feel in your heart
their promised peace that “passeth

13:37.914 --> 13:42.719 align:center line:79%
all understanding.”
In the name of Jesus Christ, amen.

